id: pm-1hbw4y
title: Nightly static quality fails closed in shallow workflow checkouts because CodeFactor parity cannot resolve a committed base
description: "The workflow-dispatch nightly checks out a single commit, while the CodeFactor parity gate requires origin/default or a local base ref to identify committed changed files. The Node 24 Ubuntu leg therefore fails before evaluating complexity even though the same gate passes in a full local checkout. Provision full Git history in validation workflows so the fail-closed gate measures the intended diff rather than treating checkout topology as a product failure."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-28T12:09:34.208Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T12:14:58.057Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#45aa267ce86ee33cac29f976"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Nightly checkout exposes the repository default-branch history needed by the CodeFactor parity gate; pnpm quality:static passes in workflow_dispatch on the feature branch; the gate remains fail-closed when neither a committed base nor worktree diff exists"
parent: pm-92if
